From 31f59db866fb42630a5c950008fd46bb77ae179d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:54:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Support multiple translation provider profiles

The single provider/model configuration becomes a list of named
profiles (provider preset, base URL, API key, model, parallel
requests and lines per request), stored as JSON in the shared
preferences. A new "Translation profile" entry at the top of the
bisub settings switches between them with one tap: every connection
field below the picker rebinds to the selected profile, and edits
there write back into it. Adding a profile starts from a copy of the
current one, so switching to another model of the same provider is
just a rename plus a new model name; profiles can be deleted after
confirmation.

The first run migrates the legacy single-provider settings into a
profile named after the provider preset, so nothing is lost. The
parallel request and batch size settings now belong to the profile,
because providers differ in how much concurrency and how large
requests they tolerate. Switching to a profile with a different
model retranslates videos on demand (the cache key includes the
model); files translated with the old model stay on disk and remain
visible in the cache browser.
